   "Halcyon-researcher": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "competing",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "compromising"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final rules are strong on reporting and recall: S1 requires 24-hour reporting for all incidents including cause-unknown and 30-day correction of previously omitted incidents, and S5 mandates recall above 8/100k with prompt notice. S2 sets a 5% permanent test-failure cap with an 18-month remediation window for existing models and customer-specific numeric results but no public publication. S3 and S4 require remote shut-off on new units after 24 months with a 6-year retrofit, and built-in fire suppression from 36 months."
 },
